<title>USA: CME seeks to trade New Zealand dollar futures.</title>
<headline>CME seeks to trade New Zealand dollar futures.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange said Friday its board passed a recommendation Wednesday to ask for regulatory approval for futures and futures-options based on the New Zealand dollar.</p>
<p>In a members' summary distributed Friday, the exchange said the proposed contracts, to be listed on the CME's International Monetary Market division, also would be available to members of the CME's Growth and Emerging Markets division for a yet-undetermined amount of time.</p>
<p>The exchange did not give further details about the contracts.</p>
<p>((DerivativesDesk(312)408-8750/E-mail:derivatives@reuters.com))</p>
